# Line endings. This is a cross-platform .NET app now - Avalonia on net10.0, built and run on Linux and
# Windows - so the rules can no longer assume Windows. CRLF in the working tree and LF in the repository
# for the Windows-authored text files, pinned here rather than left to each developer's core.autocrlf so a
# build does not depend on who checked it out.
#
# Shell scripts are the exception and must stay LF: a CRLF shebang is not a shebang, and a CRLF build.sh
# would fail on Linux with "bad interpreter". Repositories configured eol=crlf by default would otherwise
# break exactly the file a Linux user runs first.
* text=auto eol=crlf

*.cs    text eol=crlf
*.csproj text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf
*.md    text eol=crlf
*.resx  text eol=crlf
*.config text eol=crlf

*.sh    text eol=lf
